<title>USA: Tropical cyclones threaten shipping in Pacific.</title>
<headline>Tropical cyclones threaten shipping in Pacific.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two tropical cyclones are threatening shipping in the southern Pacific, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said on Monday.</p>
<p>Tropical cyclone Hina is near 23.8s/174.6w and moving southeast at 22 mph with winds of 70 mph. It is expected to weaken during the next 48 hours, while moving rapidly southeast.</p>
<p>Tropical cyclone Justin, with 75 mph winds, is in the Coral Sea, east of Australia, near 12.8s/155.3e, and is moving west-southwest at five mph.</p>
<p>It will weaken very little over the next 48 hours but may become almost stationary.</p>
